  "facts": [
    "Branisko Tunnel, 4,975 meters long, opened its first tube on June 29, 2003, after a breakthrough on May 1, 1999, marking a milestone in Slovak motorway engineering.",
    "Construction began in April 1996 with the northern tube’s exploration gallery, while the southern tube employed the New Austrian Tunnelling method, showcasing advanced tunnelling techniques of the era.",
    "With a 7.5‑meter-wide road, 1‑meter sidewalks, 4.5‑meter clearance, and a 1.2% gradient, the tunnel limits speed to 80 km/h, ensuring safe passage through the mountain pass."
